{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MAXN = 7;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int E100 = 570000004;\ntypedef long long ll;\nint n, g[MAXN][MAXN];\nll nxt[1<<MAXN][1<<MAXN];\nint bitcnt[1<<MAXN];\n\nvector<int> S[MAXN+1];\nint id[1<<MAXN];\nmap<ll, int> dp[MAXN]; \nint solve(int i, ll msk) {\n\tif (msk == 0) return 0;\n\tif (i == n) return 1;\n\tif (dp[i].find(msk) != dp[i].end()) return dp[i][msk];\n\tll ret = 0;\n\tfor (int s = 0; s < (1<<n); ++s) {\n\t\tll p = 1;\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) \n\t\t\tif (s & (1 << j)) p = g[i][j] * p % MOD;\n\t\t\telse p = (1 - g[i][j]) * p % MOD;\n\t\tll nmsk = 0;\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < 35; ++j) if ((1LL << j) & msk) nmsk |= nxt[s][S[i][j]];\n\t\tret = (ret + p * solve(i+1, nmsk)) % MOD;\n\t}\n\treturn dp[i][msk] = ret;\n}\n\nint main() {\n\tios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n\tcin.tie(nullptr);\n\tcin >> n;\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) \n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) { \n\t\t\tint x;\n\t\t\tcin >> x;\n\t\t\tg[i][j] = x * 1LL * E100 % MOD;\n\t\t}\n\tfor (int i = 1; i < (1<<n); ++i) \n\t\tbitcnt[i] = bitcnt[i ^ (i & -i)] + 1;\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < (1<<n); ++i) {\n\t\tid[i] = S[bitcnt[i]].size();\n\t\tS[bitcnt[i]].push_back(i);\n\t}\n\tfor (int i = 1; i < (1<<n); ++i) \n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < (1<<n); ++j) \n\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) \n\t\t\t\tif ((i & (1<<k)) && !(j & (1<<k)))\n\t\t\t\t\tnxt[i][j] |= 1LL << id[j|1<<k];\n\tint ans = solve(0, 1);\n\tans = (ans % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n\tcout << ans << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nE100 = 570000004\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    it = iter(input_data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    g = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            x = int(next(it))\n            g[i][j] = (x * E100) % MOD\n\n    # bitcnt for masks up to (1<<n)-1\n    bitcnt = [0]*(1<<n)\n    for mask in range(1, 1<<n):\n        bitcnt[mask] = bitcnt[mask ^ (mask & -mask)] + 1\n\n    # S[i] = list of masks with i bits set\n    S = [[] for _ in range(n+1)]\n    id = [0]*(1<<n)\n    for mask in range(1<<n):\n        cnt = bitcnt[mask]\n        id[mask] = len(S[cnt])\n        S[cnt].append(mask)\n\n    # nxt[i][j] = bitmask of indices of masks that are j with one more bit from i\n    nxt = [[0]*(1<<n) for _ in range(1<<n)]\n    for i in range(1<<n):\n        for j in range(1<<n):\n            for k in range(n):\n                if (i>>k)&1 and not (j>>k)&1:\n                    nxt[i][j] |= 1 << id[j | (1<<k)]\n\n    # dp[i] is dict mapping mask (bitmask of indices in S[i]) to result\n    dp = [dict() for _ in range(n)]\n\n    def solve_dp(i, msk):\n        if msk == 0:\n            return 0\n        if i == n:\n            return 1\n        if msk in dp[i]:\n            return dp[i][msk]\n        ret = 0\n        # iterate over all possible assignments s for row i\n        for s in range(1<<n):\n            p = 1\n            for j in range(n):\n                if (s>>j)&1:\n                    p = p * g[i][j] % MOD\n                else:\n                    p = p * ((1 - g[i][j]) % MOD) % MOD\n            nmsk = 0\n            # iterate over bits set in msk (each bit corresponds to an index in S[i])\n            for idx in range(len(S[i])):\n                if (msk>>idx)&1:\n                    nmsk |= nxt[s][S[i][idx]]\n            ret = (ret + p * solve_dp(i+1, nmsk)) % MOD\n        dp[i][msk] = ret\n        return ret\n\n    ans = solve_dp(0, 1)  # S[0] has only mask 0, id[0]=0, so msk=1 means bit0 set\n    ans = (ans % MOD + MOD) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.8410845667822286e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0007217901293188334, -0.0015683980891481042, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5759474039077759, -0.024945514276623726, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0029270683880895376, -0.023283997550606728, -0.06205803155899048, -0.05926690250635147, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.935142715112306e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.000679500459227711, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.19381403923034668, -0.004253626335412264, -0.3172591030597687, -0.04778587073087692, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.8863019347190857, -0.02975435182452202, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.2305197237292305e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00015877417172305286, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0485883504152298, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -0.0002138386043952778, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.00012337400403339416, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 